# --- runtime / build ---
runs/
/ariadne
/ariadne.exe
# Windows keeps the replaced binary as ariadne.exe~ when a build overwrites a
# running one. 20 MB of it was once committed by accident, and removed from
# the history before any push.
*~
.env
config.env
.config-*.env

# --- private: how I'm learning this, not what I built ---
# Never pushed. Keep a backup outside the repo — these are gitignored,
# so a fresh clone will NOT bring them with it.
CLAUDE.md
PROGRESS.md
# docs/* rather than docs/ — git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so the negation below only works this way.
docs/*
!docs/eval-findings.md
!docs/injection-postmortem.md
*.pdf

workspace/
# MEMORY.md is what one machine's agent happens to have learned — runtime
# state like runs/, not source. It also accumulates whatever a run was told
# to remember, which is exactly the content that should not be committed by
# reflex.
MEMORY.md
/echoserver.exe
/mcp.json
